window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["3b"]={"https://theconversation.com/canada-eu-alliance-as-a-blueprint-for-a-middle-power-bloc-it-has-a-lot-of-hurdles-to-overcome-295568":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"2d1172193cc3d85bd943adaa9d6b8c30146b9b2511c7548028c198967bc7ae22","read":"https://theconversation.com/canada-eu-alliance-as-a-blueprint-for-a-middle-power-bloc-it-has-a-lot-of-hurdles-to-overcome-295568","bytes":184979,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Canada-EU alliance: as a blueprint for a ‘middle-power bloc’ it has a lot of hurdles to overcome","by":[{"n":"Martin Waehlisch","r":"Associate Professor, University of Birmingham"},{"n":"Stefan Wolff","r":"Professor of International Security, University of Birmingham"}],"pub":"2026-11-03T16:18:15Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The dream of a Canada-EU “middle-power bloc” has hit its first serious obstacle. At the Montreal summit, Brussels failed to deliver on the promise of associate membership for Canada, despite the enthusiastic backing of European Commission president, Ursula von der Leyen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Instead, the ",["EU","https://theconversation.com/topics/european-union-eu-539"]," offered the hollow consolation of “an ever-closer association”, raising an uncomfortable question about whether the middle powers can overcome their own divisions to become a serious geopolitical force."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["two-day EU-Canada summit","https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/meetings/international-summit/2026/10/29-30/"]," culminated on October 30 with the launch of a so-called “Alliance for the Future”. That compromise formula of association, rather than associate membership – which specifically ruled out full membership – was necessary because of internal disagreements in the EU."]},{"k":"p","s":["In September, Von der Leyen, ",["offered","https://cyprus.representation.ec.europa.eu/news/2026-state-union-address-president-von-der-leyen-2026-09-16_en"]," Canada the chance to become the EU’s first “associate member”. But Germany, backed by Greece and others, ",["objected to the term","https://www.euronews.com/2026/10/27/von-der-leyens-canada-associate-membership-spurs-battle-of-words-with-eu-capitals"],", worried about legal uncertainty and the expectations it might raise in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Canadian prime minister, Mark Carney, ",["used it anyway","https://www.cp24.com/news/canada/2026/10/30/canada-european-union-close-montreal-summit-with-alliance-for-the-future-pact/"]," at the Montreal summit’s closing press conference: “Today we move toward associate membership for Canada and we launch a new alliance for the future.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carney has been unusually explicit about what he believes. In his view, the future belongs to purpose-built coalitions organised around specific interests, and the successful ones among them will grow by attracting new members."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Montreal summit fits that description. Ottawa’s ",["official account","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/news-releases/2026/10/30/canada-and-european-union-announce-new-alliance-future-create-greater"]," presents the EU-Canada Alliance for the Future as drawing on “a variable geometry of like-minded nations”. ",["According to an EU official","https://www.ft.com/content/efbe2a33-8a12-4d71-9599-26c86b9d8a0f"],", other countries have already expressed interest."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier middle-power coalitions, such as the 1997 ",["Ottawa Convention","https://www.unmas.org/sites/default/files/documents/apmbc.pdf"]," banning anti-personnel landmines, which 194 countries have ratified, ",["have shown","https://publications.gc.ca/Pilot/LoPBdP/MR/mr141-e.htm"]," that middle powers can build issue-specific leverage when a clear objective, a committed coalition and an institutional strategy line up."]},{"k":"p","s":["Can the bilateral Alliance for the Future be the nucleus around which a new middle-power coalition is built? On the one hand, a stronger Canada-EU partnership could give middle-power cooperation ",["more resources and political weight","https://www.piie.com/blogs/realtime-economics/2026/can-eu-and-canada-forge-new-partnership"],". On the other hand, the closer Ottawa and Brussels move towards each other, the harder it may be to bring in other middle powers, such as India and Brazil."]},{"k":"p","s":["The partnership’s ability to realise the ",["summit’s aspirations","https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2026/10/30/joint-statement-eu-canada-summit-30-october-2026/"]," – from digital trade to cooperation on critical resources and supercomputing – is yet to be tested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Five tests for potential success"]},{"k":"p","s":["The track record of past efforts implies five tests to judge whether Ottawa and Brussels are likely to succeed in leading a wider coalition of middle powers into a new international order."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, leadership costs money. In Montreal, Canada ",["signalled","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/statements/2026/10/30/joint-statement-canada-and-european-union-building-together-alliance"]," its “intention to join” the EU’s €90 billion (£75 billion) Ukraine support loan. That ",["will spread an existing burden","https://kyivindependent.com/canada-in-talks-to-join-eus-ukraine-loan-but-it-still-needs-to-donate-to-kyiv-eu-says/"]," rather than adding new money. The test is whether Ottawa and Brussels can mobilise new resources, not just share existing burdens."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, any middle-power coalition will need to build defence capabilities that can be sustained. Canada is the ",["first non-European participant","https://www.eunews.it/en/2026/06/15/defence-eu-countries-give-final-go-ahead-for-canadas-participation-in-safe-funding/"]," in ",["Security Action for Europe (Safe)","https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/1106/oj"],", the EU’s defence procurement scheme, and Canadian firms have won ",["contracts","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/news-releases/2026/10/30/canada-and-european-union-announce-new-alliance-future-create-greater"]," to supply radios to Poland and helmets to Latvia."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the joint statement merely “takes note” of Carney’s proposed ",["Defence, Security and Resilience Bank","https://www.canada.ca/en/department-finance/news/2026/03/canada-hosts-partners-to-advance-establishment-of-the-defence-security-and-resilience-bank.html"],", an international financial institution which would pool funds to allow it to offer loans for defence procurement for allies. This sort of thing sounds easy at summits. It gets harder once the location of headquarters, the procurement rules and memberships are at stake."]},{"k":"p","s":["Third, while military defence is important, economic defence increasingly matters as well. Any middle-power coalition will need to make economic coercion harder. The EU already has an ",["Anti-Coercion Instrument","https://policy.trade.ec.europa.eu/enforcement-and-protection/protecting-against-coercion_en"]," to respond to economic pressure from bigger powers against itself or its member states, but it does not extend the same protection to Canada."]},{"k":"p","s":["The closest to this in the ",["Montreal summit statement","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/statements/2026/10/30/joint-statement-canada-and-european-union-building-together-alliance"]," is a joint commitment to limit the “negative effects” of each side’s economic security measures on the other. That is a promise of restraint between partners, not of joint defence against a third party – even though US president Donald Trump ",["threatened tariffs","https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-09-16/trump-floats-eu-tariffs-if-canada-invite-deemed-a-hostile-act"]," on Europe if he judged associate membership for Canada to be a “hostile act”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fourth, whatever the exact vision that the EU and Canada have in mind, it needs to be built in a way that it can handle disagreement. The dispute over the “close association” versus “associate membership” did not derail the summit – but the two sides described the outcome remarkably differently."]},{"k":"p","s":["Finally, any durable middle-power coalition will need to offer a common story, and live by it. The ",["joint statement","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/statements/2026/10/30/joint-statement-canada-and-european-union-building-together-alliance"]," “deeply” regrets US sanctions on the International Criminal Court, an unusually direct rebuke of an ally. But it also leans on the language of the “rules-based international order”. Many governments in the global south treat this phrase with suspicion and prefer the ",["broader term","https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2026/09/21/declaration-of-the-partners-for-multilateralism-p4m-summit-21-september-2026/"]," international law."]},{"k":"p","s":["The difference is more than rhetorical. Defending international law would also mean upholding it when doing so conflicts with members’ own interests or those of their allies."]},{"k":"h","s":["What to watch"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Regional heavyweights","https://www.economist.com/international/2026/10/15/how-to-survive-a-predatory-world-order"]," such as Brazil, India and South Africa ",["are sceptical","https://www.economist.com/international/2026/10/15/how-to-survive-a-predatory-world-order"]," about the idea of a new post-American world order led by Europe and Canada. So the EU-Canada summit in Montreal is unlikely to have reassured them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Brussels and Ottawa will therefore have to make a conscious effort to build the issue-specific coalitions Carney favours. A possible platform to help these sorts of coalitions get off the ground was launched on the margins of the UN general assembly in September. ",["Partners for Multilateralism","https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2026/09/21/declaration-of-the-partners-for-multilateralism-p4m-summit-21-september-2026/"]," is a network to promote open international dialogue and cooperation."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was co-founded by Canada and the EU with Australia, Barbados, Brazil, India and Kenya five weeks before the Montreal summit. Whether this works will depend on three questions. What are governments prepared to pay for? What capabilities are they prepared to contribute? And what constraints on their own behaviour are they prepared to accept?"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Montreal, Canada and the EU began to answer the first two for each other. The third, which asks the most of them, they left open. It will need to be addressed if Carney’s middle-power vision is to be realised."]}],"chars":6533},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kyrgyzstan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"2729fe2881cd0fc269e913849794aa5aad083e2ac06231158ece8f4bb3966268","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/kyrgyzstan","bytes":70469,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Kyrgyzstan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-22T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-09-14T11:23:33+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kyrgyzstan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Kyrgyzstan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Kyrgyzstan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Kyrgyz Embassy in the UK","https://mfa.gov.kg/en/dm/vb"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting or resident in Kyrgyzstan, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the day you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can enter Kyrgyzstan as a visitor for stays of up to 30 calendar days without a visa, for each 60-day period. After this period expires, UK nationals must either leave Kyrgyzstan or obtain the appropriate documents."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, to work or study, see more ",["information on the available visa","https://evisa.e-gov.kg/get_information.php?lng=en"]," types."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kyrgyzstan offers an e-visa service for visitors. See ",["Kyrgyzstan’s official e-visa portal","https://www.evisa.e-gov.kg/"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting Kyrgyzstan for more than 30 calendar days, you must either leave the territory of Kyrgyzstan before the 30 calendar day period ends, or ",["register online with the State Registration Service (SRS)","https://portal.srs.kg/ru/service/e2025f78-a118-40b3-a5f5-284494b185de"]," (in Kyrgyz and Russian). You must register within 5 days of your entry into Kyrgyzstan for the period of your visa’s validity."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying with someone who owns a property in Kyrgyzstan for longer than 30 calendar days, you and the property owner must register at the State Registration Service."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not overstay your visa, or exceed your permitted duration of stay, even for a very short period. If you overstay, you could get a fine and possibly be deported. It is not always easy or possible to extend your stay or visa if you want to stay in the country for longer than planned. If you’re travelling overland, make sure you arrive at your intended border crossing in good time before your period of stay or visa expires."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Kyrgyzstan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/123/kyrgyzstan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kyrgyz-British dual nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kyrgyzstan does not recognise dual nationality. If you enter Kyrgyzstan on a Kyrgyz passport and are also a British national, the British Embassy will only be able to provide limited consular assistance. If you’re arrested or detained, the Kyrgyz authorities are unlikely to grant you access to British Embassy staff."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Kyrgyzstan (in Russian). You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bring a doctor’s prescription if you travel with prescription medicines and declare them on your customs declaration form. Some non-prescription medicines in the UK cause problems on entry into Kyrgyzstan. Possession can lead to civil or criminal proceedings if you have not declared them on arrival. Some medicines which are available without a prescription in the UK might require a prescription in Kyrgyzstan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to take any medication with you, it is recommended that you contact the Kyrgyz Embassy into the UK or a local travel agency for further advice on whether any restrictions apply to the medications you are planning to bring."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kyrgyzstan/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["regional risks advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kyrgyzstan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe abroad","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/safetyadvice/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Kyrgyzstan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Kyrgyzstan cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Be alert for any security related announcements by the Kyrgyz authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations happen regularly in Bishkek and elsewhere across the country. Most demonstrations are peaceful but can turn violent, with little or no warning. On 17 and 18 May 2024, 41 people were injured in Bishkek in Kyrgyz protests against South Asian migrant workers and students."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid crowds and demonstrations, check for updates on local media and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Street crime is a risk, including bag-snatching and mugging. Take care if you go out alone or use public transport and consider using private cars or pre-arranged taxis at night."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not show large amounts of money and be wary of strangers offering help or being over-friendly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be careful when using currency exchange offices and visiting the bazaars in Bishkek, particularly Osh Bazaar, where pickpockets target tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["Use caution and take measures to reduce your personal risk, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep sight of your belongings at all times"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of thieves using distraction techniques"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying all your valuables together in one place e.g. handbags or pockets"]},{"k":"li","s":["exercise a similar level of caution as you would in the UK"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink spiking is a risk in nightclubs and bars and can lead to sexual assault. Alcohol and drugs can reduce your vigilance, making you less in control."]},{"k":"p","s":["Buy your own drinks and always keep them in sight to avoid them being spiked. If you drink, know your limit. Avoid splitting up from your friends and do not go off with people you do not know. See ",["Travel Aware ‘Stick with your mates’","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/#stick_with_your_mates"]," for tips and advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kyrgyzstan has a secular constitution. Most Kyrgyz people are Muslim. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions. Make sure your actions do not offend other cultures or religious beliefs, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or when you visit religious sites."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. Cafés and restaurants may amend their menus and be busy around fast-breaking (‘Iftar’). Areas around mosques are also likely to be busy around prayer times. Take particular care not to offend religious sensitivities at this time."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry your passport, or a notarised copy of it, with you at all times. The police can arrest you if you do not carry ID. You can be arrested if you fail to do so. You can get a copy of your passport notarised in the UK and translated into Kyrgyz or Russian, or use a copy notarised in Kyrgyzstan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to possess or use drugs. You could get a lengthy prison sentence if convicted. Prison conditions are basic."]},{"k":"p","s":["The police conduct regular drug raids in bars and night clubs. Police will be masked and armed. Stay calm and follow instructions. If you are not carrying and have not taken drugs you are normally asked for identification and then allowed to leave."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to sell alcohol to someone aged 18 or under. Drinking in public is prohibited, and violators may face a 1,000 KGS fines or even imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["E-cigarettes"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to bring e-cigarettes, vaping devices and solutions into Kyrgyzstan or to buy and sell them. Customs officials will confiscate these items; and they could fine or detain you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Prohibited material"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is prohibited to bring certain material into Kyrgyzstan. This includes material which promotes war, terrorism, religious hatred or racism and pornographic content."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and drones in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photos of or use drones near anything related to the military or security, including border checkpoints, military sites and police stations. Check carefully that you are not near any military or security facilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you can import and use your model of drone with the Kyrgyz Embassy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be careful when posting images of your visit on social media as offence can be taken. Take particular care with images or comments about public buildings, the Kyrgyz flag, national food or customs. Disrespectful content could result in fines or detention."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are legal but not often discussed or recognised publicly. Showing affection in public could result in a violent attack or unwanted attention. Same sex marriages are not recognised in Kyrgyz law."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Power cuts"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent power cuts throughout Kyrgyzstan during the winter."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["The currency in Kyrgyzstan is the Kyrgyz som (KGS), and is usually not available in currency exchanges outside Kyrgyzstan."]},{"k":"p","s":["ATMs are widely available in main cities and usually distribute Kyrgyz som and US dollars. You should pay with KGS but USD is a universal currency, and may be accepted in certain situations. ATMs sometimes have a maximum som withdrawal limit. This varies from bank to bank, but is often around 10,000 KGS. ATMs are also usually available in smaller towns, though it may be more difficult to withdraw dollars outside main cities. Credit and debit cards are widely used around the country; VISA is accepted in most places, but MasterCard is sometimes not accepted. Payment by QR code is also common. Travellers’ cheques are not normally accepted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bring cash if you plan to travel to rural areas where ATMs may not be available."]},{"k":"p","s":["US dollars are the most easily exchanged foreign currency. Notes from before 2007 usually are not accepted or subject to additional charge if changing to Kyrgyz som."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Trekking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["Trekking in Kyrgyzstan often involves travelling to very remote areas. There is a high risk of avalanches, landslides and rockfalls. Weather can change very quickly, and heavy snowfall can block roads and trekking routes, particularly in the autumn and winter."]},{"k":"p","s":["At higher altitudes there is a possibility of snow even in the summer months, and a risk of sunstroke, serious sunburn and altitude sickness."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["get adequate insurance, including for any activity at high altitude"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a reputable trekking agency"]},{"k":"li","s":["let someone know when you plan to return"]},{"k":"li","s":["not trek alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["adapt your plans to reflect local conditions and advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["In remote areas, mobile phone or satellite phone coverage can be extremely limited. Medical facilities are basic, and difficult terrain can in some circumstances make it impossible for emergency services to reach you."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a basic mountain rescue service staffed by volunteers. The rescue equipment they have is limited. Mountain rescue 24-hour emergency number: +996 312 651 404."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive a hire car or a UK vehicle, see information on ",["driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Kyrgyzstan for up to 30 days. For stays longer than this, you’ll need to have both the 1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP) and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel. An IDP is valid for either 12 months or 3 years, depending on the type, and is issued for a fixed duration."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’re legally required to have third-party insurance. For more information, contact insurance companies in Kyrgyzstan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a minimum of one year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Kyrgyzstan. If you are tested and found to have any alcohol in your system, you may be fined and have your licence revoked for 1 year."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the police stop you and issue a fine, they should give you a paper copy with instructions on how to pay. You can pay fines through a payment terminal or in a bank. Do not pay cash directly to police officers, although some may have a payment terminal you can use. Some fines may be reduced if you pay quickly. Payment terminals are available on streets and other places such as malls, grocery stores, kiosks and restaurants."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kyrgyzstan road laws require you:"]},{"k":"li","s":["to drive on the right"]},{"k":"li","s":["to wear seatbelts for drivers and all passengers"]},{"k":"li","s":["not to use a mobile phone while driving"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many roads are poorly lit and not maintained, with road works or damaged roads often not clearly signposted. Watch out for pedestrians as they often have a low awareness of road safety. Roads outside of Bishkek are often blocked by snow in winter."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care when driving, particularly over long distances and avoid giving lifts to hitchhikers. Drivers have been robbed by people they picked up."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions can be poor in and around Bishkek, wherever possible use main roads when travelling."]},{"k":"p","s":["Petrol stations are limited in rural areas and diesel is often unavailable. Make sure you take all you need for your journey."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis and buses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid flagging down taxis. Use licensed pre-ordered taxi services whenever possible, these are more reputable and have English-speaking dispatchers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid using local buses and minibuses if possible. They are not always maintained properly and pickpockets operate on them."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["In May 2022, the UK sanctioned Aeroflot, Rossiya Airlines and Ural Airlines. It is now illegal under UK law for any British national or British company to do business with these airlines. This includes buying flight tickets."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list"]," (ASL) lists all known airlines in Kyrgyzstan that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check whether your tour operator has concerns about airlines in Kyrgyzstan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk of earthquakes and tremors are frequent. Familiarise yourself with safety procedures and follow advice from local authorities. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has information about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Avalanches and landslides"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the mountains, avalanches and landslides often block roads, particularly in the spring."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Kyrgyzstan. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kyrgyzstan/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kyrgyzstan/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kyrgyzstan-Tajikistan Border"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a history of border clashes in this area, and the security situation can change at short notice. There have been no further clashes since the border agreement in 2025. There might be a risk of unexploded ordinance and mines, particularly in the border areas of the Batken region. Border areas may be subject to sudden restrictions on movement and a heightened security presence. You should exercise caution if travelling near the Kyrgyzstan–Tajikistan border, check local conditions before travel, and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crossing the borders can be complex, take local advice if you’re planning on crossing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check local media reports before you travel to see which border posts are open. Only use officially recognised border crossings. Border crossings can close at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 103 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Kyrgyzstan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/123/kyrgyzstan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Kyrgyzstan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/123/kyrgyzstan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Kyrgyzstan. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several cases of anthrax, mainly in the south due to insufficient vaccination of animals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Air quality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Air quality in Bishkek has deteriorated due to pollutants into the air, particularly during the winter months. Try to minimise your exposure to outside air by staying in an air-conditioned indoor place as much as possible, with windows and doors closed and well-sealed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regularly damp-dust all indoor surfaces, washing your hands afterwards. Monitor local reports and weather forecasts for the latest information and advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Basic medicines including painkillers are available without a prescription. Most UK prescriptions are accepted in Kyrgyzstan, but you should phone a Kyrgyz pharmacy in advance to check. You may need to get your UK prescription translated into Russian or Kyrgyz. You can get a translation in Kyrgyzstan – ",["find an interpreter or translator","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Kyrgyzstan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some prescription medications are not widely available. Medications often come under different brand names, so ask for the drug’s generic name. If your medication is not available, you may be able to get it couriered from Russia or Turkey, though this could take time."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need to pay cash for medication."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Kyrgyzstan"]},{"k":"p","s":["The quality of medical care in Kyrgyzstan is not as high as the UK. Medical facilities are often badly equipped and unhygienic, with a limited supply of drugs. There is no guarantee that equipment will have been properly sterilised, especially in rural hospitals. Avoid all but basic or essential treatment in the event of an emergency. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no reciprocal healthcare agreement between the UK and Kyrgyzstan."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Kyrgyzstan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kyrgyzstan-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Kyrgyzstan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 103"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 101"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 102"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rescue and emergency: 112"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tourist police in Issyk-Kul Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Issyk-Kul Oblast (province) and need help, you can call the tourist police call centre, where the staff speak English and Russian, or message on WhatsApp, on +996 705 00 91 02."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Kyrgyzstan"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Kyrgyzstan"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Kyrgyzstan"]," in Kyrgyzstan"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Kyrgyzstan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kyrgyzstan-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Kyrgyzstan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kyrgyzstan-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/kyrgyzstan/british-embassy-bishkek"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kyrgyzstan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re considering investing or doing business in Kyrgyzstan, it is important to research carefully."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there are British companies operating successfully in Kyrgyzstan, there have been instances of British people getting into difficulties. This includes having assets stolen or being physically attacked. See Kyrgyzstan’s ranking in the ",["Transparency International Global Corruption Index","https://www.transparency.org/en/cpi/2022"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Kyrgyz legal system can be slow and getting judgements implemented can be very difficult. The British Embassy is not able to get involved (including offering advice) in private disputes over property, employment, commercial or other matters."]},{"k":"p","s":["Business associations in Kyrgyzstan may be able to offer you advice. If you get into difficulties due to the actions of state bodies, you can also contact the ",["Kyrgyzstan ombudsman","https://ombudsman.kg/index.php?option=com_content&view=category&layout=blog&id=114&filter_tag%5b0%5d=&Itemid=176&lang=en"]," (in Russian and Kyrgyz)."]}],"chars":22664,"change":"Removal of information about the World Nomad Games ('Warnings and insurance' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/forms-phone-calls-and-portals-the-hidden-work-that-keeps-american-institutions-functioning-burdens-parents-most-288255":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"9c6c5b22b03c9a61e1bbf2d7b474665d557511755ba9a8daa487141710b94e21","read":"https://theconversation.com/forms-phone-calls-and-portals-the-hidden-work-that-keeps-american-institutions-functioning-burdens-parents-most-288255","bytes":185692,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Forms, phone calls and portals: The hidden work that keeps American institutions functioning burdens parents most","by":[{"n":"Lauren Hall","r":"Professor of Political Science and Associate Dean, Rochester Institute of Technology; Institute for Humane Studies"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T13:39:54Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["As a working mom of three kids, I spend a lot of time parenting. I also spend a lot of time coordinating insurance, physician and school forms and remembering passwords to six different school and sports portals. None of that is really parenting, and it’s not paid work either, but it takes time away from both."]},{"k":"p","s":["I’m also a ",["political theorist who studies","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=oIjvUQsAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao"]," how institutional design affects people’s daily lives. What many people characterize as unavoidable aspects of modern life actually provide important lessons about how various institutions are set up and who does the work to keep them functional."]},{"k":"h","s":["Which institutions?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most American families deal with multiple complex institutions every week: a personalized mix of health insurers and medical providers, schools, tax authorities, Social Security and benefits agencies, daycares and camps and other kid activities, and state and federal programs such as Medicaid or SNAP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Each of these programs has its own logic, including specific rules, portals, databases, forms, deadlines and definitions. This variation creates subtle misalignments across programs that compound over time. The physician needs prior authorization from the insurer, but the insurer claims the doctor needs a specific form. Meanwhile, the school needs the doctor’s document, and a benefits office might need proof that another agency already has in its system."]},{"k":"p","s":["The people working to align all these systems ",["are parents","https://www.pewresearch.org/social-trends/2026/06/16/for-working-parents-the-boundary-between-work-and-family-is-often-blurred/"],", often people with the ",["least time and cognitive availability","https://www.hhs.gov/surgeongeneral/reports-and-publications/parents/index.html"]," to handle the burden."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political scientists ",["Pamela Herd","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=EaMwa3wAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao"]," and ",["Donald Moynihan","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=-8qHKqUAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao"]," of the ",["Better Government Lab","https://www.bettergovernmentlab.org/"]," call this load ",["administrative burden","https://doi.org/10.1093/jopart/muu009"],"; that burden includes learning all the rules, figuring out how to comply with them, and then handling all the rippling demands that each individual task creates."]},{"k":"p","s":["These burdens are not natural or inevitable. Instead, they’re the result of the way people have designed our institutions. The good news is that it’s possible to do things differently."]},{"k":"h","s":["How did we get here?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most institutions weren’t intentionally designed with the user experience in mind. Instead, they’re the result of piecemeal decisions over decades, often the ",["result of a complex interplay","https://www.hachettebookgroup.com/titles/paul-starr/the-social-transformation-of-american-medicine/9780465093021/"]," of interest-group lobbying, political jockeying and public demands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Employer-based health insurance resulted, in part, from ",["fear of socialized medicine","https://www.npr.org/2020/10/07/921287295/history-of-employer-based-health-insurance-in-the-u-s"]," during World War II. Public schools grew out of local communities and then had ",["layers of state and federal regulations","https://www.ebsco.com/research-starters/history/history-public-education-us"]," piled on top. Bureaucracies at different levels and of different types rarely talk to each other or bother coordinating their rules and processes."]},{"k":"p","s":["And most of these rules and processes aren’t usually ",["nefarious in intent","https://www.russellsage.org/publications/book/administrative-burden"],". Documentation can prevent fraud, eligibility rules help allocate scarce resources, regulations can protect patients, and institutions have a vested interest in protecting themselves from mistakes and liability."]},{"k":"p","s":["But each operates in isolation. The cracks are visible only to the person who has to navigate these silos – and that’s often an overextended parent."]},{"k":"h","s":["Who pays (more)?"]},{"k":"p","s":["It might seem like everyone bears the same administrative burdens, but they don’t. Life administration hits some groups harder than others; ",["women","https://doi.org/10.1177/0003122419859007"],", ",["people with disabilities","https://www.americanprogress.org/article/how-dehumanizing-administrative-burdens-harm-disabled-people/"]," and ",["lower-income people","https://doi.org/10.7758/RSF.2023.9.5.01"]," all interact more frequently with these fragmented systems and are less able to absorb the costs of those interactions."]},{"k":"p","s":["For a middle-class American on salary, an hour on hold is a nuisance. For a waitress working for tips, it’s lost earnings or even lost employment. For many Americans, the administrative burden of applying for and proving eligibility for benefits is dramatic; the people who need these programs the most ",["struggle to access them","https://www.harpercollins.com/products/the-time-tax-annie-lowrey"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is what researchers call a regressive effect in public policy, meaning that the costs hit hardest for those who can least afford it. Many institutions are effectively means-tested in reverse: The most vulnerable pay the most in terms of time, energy and money."]},{"k":"h","s":["How to align fragmented systems"]},{"k":"p","s":["While there is no easy fix with institutions as complex as healthcare, education or public benefits, there are some options."]},{"k":"p","s":["One useful model is ",["universal design","https://universaldesign.ie/about-universal-design"],": the idea that we should build our environments – in this case, institutions – for people of different abilities from the start."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the institutional front, this would mean more flexible hours to accommodate a range of users; a combination of email, phone and platform access; automatic enrollment or renewal when eligibility is already known; various plain language rules; and agencies sharing information, with permission, and working together to resolve conflicts between policies and rules so families aren’t forced into the role of unpaid institutional coordinators. Much of this will require not just language rewrites but ",["significant investment in new systems","https://www.recodingamerica.us/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Michigan provides an example of reform working at scale. In 2018 the state ",["consolidated benefit application forms","https://digitalgovernmenthub.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/Large-Scale-Human-Centered-Redesign.pdf"]," across five programs, reducing length and complexity. The original combined application packet was an overwhelming 1,000 questions and over 64 pages long."]},{"k":"p","s":["The streamlined application process, which could be completed in about 20 minutes, not only improved the process for those applying. It reduced errors, cut down worker processing time and saved caseworkers 200,000 hours per year, presumably saving tax dollars along the way. Reducing administrative burden across programs is one of the few policy reforms with almost no downside."]},{"k":"p","s":["For now, many Americans are like fish swimming in polluted water. We know something’s wrong, but we can’t see the cause. The next time you’re stuck on hold trying to fix a paperwork error with one agency before you can submit additional paperwork to another, it’s worthwhile to remember that this experience isn’t an inevitability of modern life. It’s the result of design choices – or failure to make choices – that can be changed."]}],"chars":5898},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/yemen":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"d38272eb993c4a4292fc5c9719ccc0f11168548a02b2d280db674dd2ba8ec364","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/yemen","bytes":49024,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Yemen travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-19T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-27T16:06:42+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Yemen"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the whole of the Yemen due to the unpredictable security conditions."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Yemen, you should leave immediately."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/yemen/safety-and-security"]," for more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["UK government support"]},{"k":"p","s":["Support for British people is severely limited in Yemen. British Embassy services in Sana’a are suspended, and all diplomatic and consular staff have been withdrawn."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK government cannot help British nationals leaving Yemen. There are no evacuation procedures in place."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO cannot offer advice on the safety of travelling to any potential departure point. The UK government’s ability to help with onward travel is severely limited and you’ll be expected to cover the cost of visas, accommodation, insurance and onward travel yourself."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to remain in Yemen, you should minimise movement around the country and within cities and towns, monitor developments in the local security situation and follow other precautions in this travel advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British national in Yemen and need help from the UK government, you can call FCDO on 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and US military infrastructure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since July 2026, the Houthis have launched air strikes against Saudi territory and Saudi shipping vessels in the Red Sea. There is an ongoing risk of further military escalation, including in Yemen and the Red Sea, which could occur at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to FCDO Travel Advice ",["email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/yemen/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information, including updates relating to airports and airspace which could close at short notice"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure. Do not approach or touch any drone or missile fragments or unusual objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel against FCDO advice, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/yemen/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK who choose to travel against FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Yemen’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Yemen set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Yemeni Embassy in the UK","https://www.yemenembassy.co.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Yemen, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Yemen."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Apply for a visa through the ",["Yemeni Embassy in the UK","https://www.yemenembassy.co.uk/visa"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Yemen guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/246/yemen#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you visit Yemen for more than 14 days, you must register your passport with the Yemen immigration authorities after you arrive."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Yemen. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into and out of Yemen"]},{"k":"p","s":["Import and export of local currency is illegal. There are no restrictions on the import of foreign currencies, but you must declare amounts higher than 3,000 US dollars. Export of foreign currencies must not exceed the amount imported."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are not many ATMs outside of Sana’a. US dollars in cash is the most easily convertible currency."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Yemen"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Yemen."]},{"k":"p","s":["The threat is heightened where Al-Qaida in the Arabian Peninsula (AQAP) and Islamic State-Yemen have tribal connections and in the governorates of Abyan, Marib, Hadramawt and Shabwah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Western and Houthi interests in Yemen remain a feature in AQAP propaganda, and AQAP views westerners and Houthi as legitimate targets for attacks. Terrorist attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels and supermarkets"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport routes"]},{"k":"li","s":["oil and gas infrastructure"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["gatherings"]},{"k":"li","s":["airports and transport hubs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks targeting or affecting British nationals of Yemeni origin cannot be ruled out. Attacks against Yemeni security forces and Houthis are on the rise throughout the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Methods of attack have included:"]},{"k":"li","s":["attacks by militants"]},{"k":"li","s":["firearm assassinations"]},{"k":"li","s":["kidnappings"]},{"k":"li","s":["improvised explosive devices and car bombs left in buildings and roadways"]},{"k":"li","s":["suicide attacks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Daesh-Yemen has conducted multiple terrorist attacks across the country, including Aden, Sana’a, Ibb, Hodeida and al-Bayda. So far this has been focussed on Houthi, security forces and the Yemeni government but western interests are highly likely to be regarded as targets."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a very high and constant threat of kidnap across Yemen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Al-Qaida in the Arabian Peninsula (AQAP) propaganda has called for continued kidnapping of westerners. However, armed tribes and criminal groups have also carried out kidnaps in the past. There is a high risk that such groups would sell any hostages on to AQAP, who have murdered a number of hostages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kidnaps have occurred at various times of day and in a wide variety of locations, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["public places in the capital"]},{"k":"li","s":["cars while travelling"]},{"k":"li","s":["victims’ accommodation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kidnapping attempts often involve the use of force and have ended in the death of several victims."]},{"k":"p","s":["All British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, NGOs, humanitarian aid workers, journalists, business travellers, and long-term residents. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is not to make substantive concessions to terrorist hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political and security situation in Yemen remains uncertain and volatile."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since April 2022 a de-facto ceasefire has remained in place between the Houthis and the Yemeni government. On 23 December 2023, the UN announced that the Houthis and internationally recognised government of Yemen had committed to a ceasefire. However, sporadic incidents continue to occur along frontlines and the security situation remains volatile. Due to ongoing hostilities in the Red Sea, there is a heightened state of alert across Yemen and widescale conflict may resume at short notice. In February, in response to US and UK airstrikes, the Houthi authorities designated the US and UK as ‘hostile states’."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a result, we strongly advise against all travel to Houthi controlled areas. The risk of attack to British nationals also extends to areas under Yemeni government control."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reports of arbitrary arrests and enforced disappearances raise concerns. The Houthis have arrested opponents, including politicians, journalists, academics and activists. British nationals have also been detained by Houthis in the past, including aid workers working for NGOs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Regularly reassess your security arrangements and carefully plan your movements if travelling within Yemen. Avoid keeping the same routine by changing routes you use and keeping a low profile at all times. Follow health and security advice given by Yemen authorities and security experts before any travel in the country. Always check routes in advance and do not advertise your plans on social media. Military weapons are readily available and may be used by criminals and terrorists or in security operations. The risk of crime, such as carjacking, robbery or extortion, is widespread throughout the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tribal disputes over land are common and may involve the use of weapons. The Houthis and other militias run extra-judicial detention centres and arbitrary detention is widespread. Following recent events in the Red Sea there is an especially high risk of British nationals being detained."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yemen is an Islamic country with Islamic law. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions, particularly during the holy month of Ramadan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country and you should check this before you travel. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Men and women must wear loose-fitting clothing that covers down to the elbow and reaches below the knees. You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid tight-fitting clothing"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid clothes with profane slogans or images"]},{"k":"li","s":["not wear clothing with symbols or slogans that could be viewed as political as this could lead to arrest"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not drink alcohol in public."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taking pictures in or around military sites is likely to result in arrest and arbitrary detention. British consular services will not be able to offer support in this situation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take pictures of people without their consent."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Consensual same-sex relations are illegal in Yemen, with penalties including fines, corporal punishment, imprisonment and the death penalty."]},{"k":"p","s":["In January and February 2024, criminal courts in northern Yemen reportedly sentenced 20 individuals to death for homosexuality. A further 26 were sentenced to flogging and prison terms of between 6 months and 10 years on charges of ‘spreading immorality’ and ‘immoral acts’."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Antiquities"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get permission from the General Authority for Antiquities before exporting or removing antiques from Yemen. It’s illegal to remove or sell Yemeni antiques without permission."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Yemen, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are poor and mountain roads are dangerous. Avoid all road travel outside the main cities at night. Landmines from the current and previous conflicts are a risk on Yemen’s roads. Make sure to go with an experienced guide if you’re travelling off well-used tracks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access routes in and out of major cities may be closed or blocked. Always check the road is open before starting your journey."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a severe shortage of fuel in Yemen."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yemen’s airspace is currently controlled by Saudi-led coalition forces. Prior permission from the coalition must be obtained before flying."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The conflict extends to Yemeni territorial waters off the Red Sea and the Bab-Al Mandab Strait. Houthi forces present an ongoing risk to all shipping in the Red Sea and the Bab-Al Mandab Strait due to the potential for misidentification and miscalculation by Houthi forces."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Piracy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Piracy in the Gulf of Aden continues to be a threat. For more information and advice, see ",["piracy and armed robbery at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclones sometimes affect parts of the country. Monitor local and international weather updates."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 191 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the current conflict, emergency services may not be able to respond. It may be better to make your own way to hospital if you can. Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Yemen","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/246/yemen#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Yemen","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/246/yemen"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Middle East respiratory syndrome"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Yemen. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Yemen"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities, particularly away from the main towns and cities, are poor. Make sure that you have adequate travel health insurance and access to funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Yemen"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a result of the conflict, emergency services in Yemen have severely limited capacity and are highly unreliable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 191"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 191"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 199 or 194"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers in Yemen","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=yemen"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death abroad","https://www.gov.uk/after-a-death/death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Yemen","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/yemen-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/yemen/british-embassy-sana-a"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/yemen/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":17599,"change":"Updated information about regional tensions (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)"},"https://theconversation.com/robert-pattinson-is-the-first-bond-with-a-strong-franchise-history-it-makes-him-a-safe-choice-296872":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T20:22Z","sha":"d4cf630b9cfba20870cc93be3d7097418a30b6d99ff44e2e7284bc53706aeb75","read":"https://theconversation.com/robert-pattinson-is-the-first-bond-with-a-strong-franchise-history-it-makes-him-a-safe-choice-296872","bytes":176463,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Robert Pattinson is the first Bond with a strong franchise history – it makes him a safe choice","by":[{"n":"Yannis Tzioumakis","r":"Professor of Film and Media Industries, University of Liverpool"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T15:25:02Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Robert Pattinson’s casting as the new Bond has been met with a mixed reaction across the internet."]},{"k":"p","s":["For some, he has the looks and he can do action. He’s proven he can handle all kinds of villains who dream of world domination from the plotting, power-hungry Antinous in Christopher Nolan’s ",["The Odyssey","https://theconversation.com/topics/the-odyssey-58932"]," (2026) to corrupt, manipulative preacher Preston Teagardin in The Devil All the Time (2020)."]},{"k":"p","s":["I am not as convinced. But I was also happy to see someone cast that I’ve had good knowledge of as an actor. Perhaps more importantly, I was relieved to see that the choice involved a man who was in his 40s (only just). Being both a big fan of the series and much closer to Daniel Craig’s age myself, I was afraid that the new producers of the franchise would go down the (much) younger actor route."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Bond series has historically been attracting ",["more discerning and mature audiences","https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/mono/10.4324/9780203030769-8/new-hollywood-new-millennium-thomas-schatz-warren-buckland"]," than the Marvel and DC films or even the Star Wars franchise. I can imagine it might have been tempting for Amazon to try to entice the much coveted youth demographic through the choice of a young(er) Bond."]},{"k":"p","s":["Still, the decision to cast Pattinson doesn’t seem to have been either easy or obvious. This is the first Bond played by an actor who was once a teen idol. It’s also the first Bond who has been a member of multiple other cinematic universes: from the Wizarding World (with a small but memorable part in Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire) and the ",["Twilight Saga","https://theconversation.com/topics/twilight-3466"]," (which he largely defined through his role as Edward Cullen) to the ",["Batman Epic Crime Saga","https://theconversation.com/the-batman-the-dark-knight-on-screen-has-always-reflected-contemporary-tastes-178481"]," (as the titular superhero) and the ",["Dune universe","https://theconversation.com/topics/dune-43718"]," (portraying Scytale in the third instalment of that franchise). Now to the Bond universe."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pattinson’s ability to seamlessly integrate himself into so many major story-worlds, in small parts and leading roles, as a hero and a villain, speaks volumes both to his skills as an actor and the characteristics of his star persona. He has proven himself an actor who is not as easy to pin down, especially when taking into consideration his more indie roles."]},{"k":"p","s":["He’s had memorable performances in A24 titles such as The Lighthouse (2019), ",["The Drama","https://theconversation.com/the-1930s-and-40s-were-the-golden-age-of-the-remarriage-comedy-the-drama-and-the-invite-are-their-dark-progeny-288823"]," (2026) and ",["Primetime","https://theconversation.com/primetime-in-this-taut-morally-complex-thriller-ambition-entertainment-and-justice-collide-295303"]," (2026) and collaborations with art-house auteurs such as Bong Joon Ho ( ",["Mickey 17","https://theconversation.com/mickey-17-this-absurdist-dystopian-clone-drama-is-highly-entertaining-despite-its-flaws-251496"],", 2025), David Cronenberg (Cosmopolis, 2012) and Fernando Meirelles (the upcoming The Take, 2027). These stints paint a picture of a highly unpredictable actor who can be at home in any kind of a project. The choices Pattinson makes with his projects speaks to his artistic sensibilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["So he’s a global star and an indie darling. He’s the seasoned franchise professional and the artist with the ability to regenerate with every role. He’s also the 40-year old ( ",["although he claims he’s gen Z","https://www.youtube.com/shorts/mD72FAKoQW8"],") who appeals to adults while continuing to have an extremely strong fan-base among young audiences – a performer approved by both children and parents."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is perhaps such intriguing combinations that convinced Amazon MGM to cast him in the role of Bond. In doing so, Amazon went against long-standing casting practices in the franchise’s history of casting actors who were not incredibly well known yet or associated with other such well known characters or franchises."]},{"k":"p","s":["Having had so far mixed results in extending franchises ( ",["The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power","https://theconversation.com/rings-of-power-in-an-age-of-epic-fantasy-on-screen-many-of-the-missteps-are-unforgivable-190106"]," and Reacher) and with its production strategies increasingly focused on exploiting established intellectual property (with ",["a reboot of Robocop","https://collider.com/prime-video-robocop-reboot-series-plot-details/"]," also in development), Amazon could not afford to get Bond wrong. Casting Pattinson is a calculated risk that also fits well with the big tech company’s well-publicised identity as an ",["innovator","https://www.london.edu/think/diie-innovation-icons-amazon"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Casting Pattinson as 007 may not have been an obvious move, but it was the product of thinking outside the box and against established practices in the series and, arguably, in franchise casting more broadly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Should the 26th Bond film be a box office hit and the entry point to a new chapter in the franchise’s history, it could be down to this clever pairing of a star for all seasons and a company that recognised his qualities and cast him (kind of) against the grain."]}],"chars":4093}};
